{%- assign home_url = site.home_url | default: "/" -%}
{%- comment -%}
  The home page is reachable at BOTH "/" and "/index.html" — the file is
  index.html, and the host serves it for the bare path too. The menu's "Home"
  and "Roles You Can Play" items are bare anchors (#site-top), which have to be
  prefixed with the home address from every OTHER page and left bare on the
  home page itself, or clicking them reloads instead of scrolling. So the test
  is "is this the home page", not a string compare against one of its two
  addresses: `page.url` is whichever one Eleventy wrote.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign on_home = false -%}
{%- if page.url == "/" or page.url == "/index.html" or page.url == home_url -%}
  {%- assign on_home = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Which menu item is lit. A page is normally its own menu item, but a section
  with sub-pages — Resources has eighteen — wants the parent item lit on every
  one of them, the way ondc.org does it. Such a page sets `nav_active` in its
  front matter to the menu address it belongs under.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign active_url = nav_active | default: page.url -%}
<div data-visible="true" id="site-header">
  <nav class="navbar">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="nav-logo" href="{{ home_url }}#site-top"><img
          alt="{{ site.logo_alt }}"
          src="{{ site.logo }}"
          style="height: 52px; width: auto; display: block;"/></a>
      <div class="nav-links">
        {% for item in site.nav %}{% if item.children %}{%- comment -%}A drop-down is "active" when the page we are on is one of its children — the same rule the plain links use one branch down, just applied to the whole group.{%- endcomment -%}{% assign drop_active = "" %}{% for child in item.children %}{% if child.url == active_url %}{% assign drop_active = " active" %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}<details class="nav-drop"><summary class="nav-link{{ drop_active }}">{{ item.label }}<svg
                  aria-hidden="true"
                  class="nav-drop-chev"
                  fill="none"
                  height="5"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  stroke-width="1.4"
                  viewbox="0 0 8 5"
                  width="8"><path d="M1 1l3 3 3-3"></path></svg></summary><div class="nav-drop-menu">{% for child in item.children %}<a href="{{ child.url }}"{% if child.url == active_url %} class="active"{% endif %}>{{ child.label }}</a>{% endfor %}</div></details>{% else %}{% assign first_char = item.url | slice: 0 %}{% if first_char == "#" and on_home == false %}{% assign href = home_url | append: item.url %}{% else %}{% assign href = item.url %}{% endif %}<a
              class="nav-link{% if item.url == active_url %} active{% endif %}"
              href="{{ href }}"{% if item.new_tab %} rel="noopener"
              target="_blank"{% endif %}>{{ item.label }}</a>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="nav-right">
        <button class="nav-cta" onclick="window.open('{{ site.cta_url }}', '_blank', 'noopener')">{{ site.cta_label }}</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>
</div>
